{"id":"neet-2022r-q070","pn":70,"y":"Re-NEET 2022 · 4 Sep","tp":"Hydrocarbons","st":"Boiling points of alkanes","q":"The decreasing order of boiling points of the following alkanes is :\n(a) heptane (b) butane (c) 2-methylbutane (d) 2-methylpropane (e) hexane\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :","o":["(a) > (e) > (c) > (b) > (d)","(a) > (c) > (e) > (d) > (b)","(c) > (d) > (a) > (e) > (b)","(a) > (e) > (b) > (c) > (d)"],"c":0,"s":"Boiling point rises with molar mass.\nAt equal carbon count, a straight chain boils higher than a branched one.\nHeptane has the highest molar mass; 2-methylpropane is small and branched, so lowest.\nOrder: heptane > hexane > 2-methylbutane > butane > 2-methylpropane."},
{"id":"neet-2022r-q097","pn":97,"y":"Re-NEET 2022 · 4 Sep","tp":"Hydrocarbons","st":"Preparation of alkenes","q":"The incorrect method for the synthesis of alkenes is :","o":["treating vicinal dihalides with Zn metal","treatment of alkynes with Na in liquid NH₃","heating alkyl halides with alcoholic KOH","treating alkyl halides in aqueous KOH solution"],"c":3,"s":"Vicinal dihalides with Zn give alkenes (dehalogenation).\nAlkynes with Na in liquid NH₃ give trans alkenes.\nAlkyl halides with alcoholic KOH give alkenes by elimination.\nAlkyl halides with aqueous KOH give alcohols by substitution, so this is the incorrect method.","sfig":{"w":495,"h":225,"alt":"Four reactions: R-Cl with aqueous KOH gives R-OH; 2-chlorobutane with alcoholic KOH gives but-2-ene and but-1-ene; an alkyne with Na in liquid NH3 gives a trans alkene; a vicinal dihalide with Zn gives ethene.","d":[["t",14,20,"(4) R–Cl",""],["l",75,16.5,142.5,16.5,"a"],["t",107.5,8,"aq KOH","ms"],["t",150,20,"R–OH",""],["t",14,71.5,"(3) CH₃–CH–CH–CH₃",""],["l",105,47.5,105,58.5,""],["t",107.5,40.5,"Cl","m"],["l",170,67.5,212.5,67.5,"a"],["t",191,57,"alc","ms"],["t",191,87,"KOH","ms"],["t",219,71.5,"CH₃–CH=CH–CH₃ + CH₃–CH₂–CH=CH₂",""],["t",14,119,"(2) R–C ≡ C–R",""],["l",117.5,108.5,162.5,108.5,"a"],["t",139,102,"Na","ms"],["t",139,130,"Liq NH₃","ms"],["l",182.5,106.5,197.5,116,""],["l",182.5,126,197.5,116,""],["t",175,105.5,"R","m"],["t",175,131.5,"R","m"],["t",212.5,120,"C=C","m"],["l",227.5,116,243.5,106,""],["l",227.5,116,243.5,126,""],["t",251,105.5,"R","m"],["t",251,131.5,"R","m"],["t",76.5,153,"X","m"],["l",76.5,159,76.5,170,""],["t",14,184,"(1) CH₂–CH₂",""],["l",41.5,191.5,41.5,202.5,""],["t",41.5,215.5,"X","m"],["l",102.5,180,150,180,"a"],["t",125,170.5,"Zn","ms"],["t",125,199,"Metal","ms"],["t",157.5,184,"CH₂= CH₂",""]]}},
{"id":"neet-2022-q098","pn":98,"y":"NEET 2022 · 17 Jul","tp":"Hydrocarbons","st":"Ozonolysis of alkenes","q":"Compound X on reaction with O₃ followed by Zn/H₂O gives formaldehyde and 2-methyl propanal as products. The compound X is","o":["2-Methylbut-1-ene","2-Methylbut-2-ene","Pent-2-ene","3-Methylbut-1-ene"],"c":3,"s":"Reductive ozonolysis cuts the C=C bond and puts C=O on each carbon.\nJoin the two products back at the carbonyl carbons: HCHO and (CH₃)₂CHCHO.\nThis gives CH₂=CH–CH(CH₃)₂, which is 3-methylbut-1-ene.","sfig":{"w":360,"h":224,"alt":"Products 2-methylpropanal and formaldehyde (top), and 3-methylbut-1-ene with (i) O3 then (ii) Zn/H2O giving them (bottom)","d":[["l",176,60,197,48,""],["l",197,48,218,60,""],["l",197,48,197,24,""],["l",216,60,216,76,""],["l",220,60,220,76,""],["t",218,88,"O","m"],["l",218,60,234,50,""],["t",240,51,"H","m"],["t",252,66,"+","m"],["l",294,62,294,46,""],["l",290,62,290,46,""],["t",292,42,"O","m"],["l",292,62,278,72,""],["l",292,62,306,72,""],["t",272,79,"H","m"],["t",312,79,"H","m"],["t",208,106,"2-Methylpropanal","ms"],["t",292,106,"Formaldehyde","ms"],["l",14,170,35,158,""],["l",35,158,56,170,""],["l",56,170,77,158,""],["l",57.5,164.5,71.5,156.5,""],["l",35,158,35,134,""],["t",50,212,"3-Methylbut-1-ene","ms"],["l",104,176,160,176,"a"],["t",132,162,"(i) O₃","ms"],["t",132,192,"(ii) Zn/H₂O","ms"],["l",176,170,197,158,""],["l",197,158,218,170,""],["l",197,158,197,134,""],["l",216,170,216,186,""],["l",220,170,220,186,""],["t",218,198,"O","m"],["l",218,170,234,160,""],["t",240,161,"H","m"],["t",252,176,"+","m"],["l",294,172,294,156,""],["l",290,172,290,156,""],["t",292,152,"O","m"],["l",292,172,278,182,""],["l",292,172,306,182,""],["t",272,189,"H","m"],["t",312,189,"H","m"]]}}
